speechtext:
The requirements for eligibility for financing which I gave last night are set out in a pamphlet entitled "Government Export Financing" and also at page 16 of the pamphlet entitled, "Export Credits Insurance Corporation, What it is and How it Operates". In the first pamphlet "Eligibility for Financing" they are set out in this way:
The guiding rules that determine the eligibility of transactions for financing are:
1.	that the extended credit terms are clearly necessary and justifiable;

Farm Credit Act
2.	that the transaction gives promise of continuing export trade;
3.	that the Canadian content is of a high order, in the range of 80 per cent or better;
4.	that the transaction gives rise to significant employment and industrial benefits in Canada;
5.	that the export transaction is substantial in value;
6.	that the foreign buyer and the country of purchase have a satisfactory credit standing.
